hey guys I'm Abby start welcome to  Abby's kitchen today i parted up with my  friends at Wonderful Pistachios who  sponsored this video help Canadians  coast-to-coast elevate their roadtrip  snacking game if you're traveling  anywhere in the summer chances are going  to be stuck in the car for at least a  few hours and you're going to get pretty  hungry  whenever I plan my road trips I stick to  four pieces criteria for my road trip  snacks number one they can't be messy  unless it's not your car and you don't  care about the detailing number two  they've got to be shelf stable because  as we know in Canada our cities are far  away from one another in the great white  north number three they cannot be smelly  because six hours in the car with tuna  or egg salad sandwich not ideal and  number four they've got to be tasty that  one's the most important of course  pistachios check off all the boxes all  in their own so I always spit bag of  them in my car just ready to go  but I also like to switch things up to  elevate my road trip snacking games so  I'm also adding them to an pre favorite  road trip recipes let's do this first up  my matcha energy balls with a great pop  of color and flavor from pistachios into  a food processor I combined some  unsalted shells Wonderful Pistachios  some dates some unclean coconut rolled  oats ground flax seeds nacho powder  coconut oil and dry cranberries puree  until well combined your dates aren't  sticky enough you may want to add a  little bit of maple syrup agave or honey  then roll into a bed a dozen balls and  keep refrigerated until you're ready for  your road trip  next my thai-inspired popcorn pistachio  trail next by mixing it up and adding  sweet chili pistachios we can up our  snacking game with a big pick of flavor  I mixed together some air-popped popcorn  sweet chili wonderful pistachios and  some diced apricots toss with a little  bit of olive oil and sprinkle with some  coconut sugar curry powder ginger lime  zest salt and pepper transfer to two  baggie for snacking on your road trip  finally my pistachio protein oak bites  please provide a satisfying and tasty  crunch to elevate traditional granola  cups first I preheat my oven to 325  degrees Fahrenheit and lightly grease 24  mini muffin tins then in a bowl I  combine some rolled oats freeze dried  berries unsalted shelled pistachios hemp  hearts cinnamon nutmeg and salt in a  saucepan i combined some vanilla protein  powder unsweetened orange juice maple  syrup and coconut oil and stir over  medium heat until begins to bubble and  is very smooth then I just finish it off  with a hit of vanilla pour the protein  powder mixture over the dry ingredients  and stir until everything is well coated  place about two tablespoons into each of  the mini muffin tins and pack it flat  into the bottom of the tin finish it off  with a sprinkle of hemp hearts some  freeze-dried berry crumbs and some  pistachio crumb bake the mixture in your  preheated oven for 15 to 16 minutes  until golden brown and allow the bites  to cool completely  for carefully removing them from the tin  I store my oke bites in an airtight  container for about a week  or I pop them into freezer bags for as  much as three months until I'm ready for  my road trip  thanks again to wonderful two stashes  for sponsoring this video if you like  these recipes be sure to give this video  the thumbs up leave me a comment below  some of your favorite roadtrip snacks  subscribe to the channel and I'll see  you next time on Abby's kitchen happy  road tripping  [Music]
 

